  "notes": "A ten-man over-the-top-rope battle royal for the vacant, inaugural RWF National Championship closed the card (recounted in prose rather than structured as a two-sided match): Tyrone Parker, fired days earlier, entered in disguise as a \"mystery man\" and won, eliminating (in order) Matt Blazer, Eric Cooper, Steel Jordan (eliminated by his own tag partner, Metal Jackson), Metal Jackson, Darren Henry, Tower, Kevin Anderson, Pirate Jean Jacque Lamaire, and finally Ravage. Shane Alexander, injured the prior week, was replaced by Tower; the fired Tyrone Parker was nominally replaced by Kevin Anderson before revealing himself as the disguised tenth entrant. The World Title Tournament's semifinal and final, and the fed's own planned 25 October pay-per-view (\"Dead... or Alive!!\"), are not attested in the held record."
